---
smd: 1
title: What spec v2 reads differently
summary: Pins how v1 reads what Styled Markdown 2.0 rejects or reinterprets (mismatched closers, duplicate attributes, conflicting titles, braces after a heading, include sections found by a part of their text, and the priority of an agent block), so later releases are compared against them.
status: draft
updated: 2026-10-15
---

## Mismatched closers

Each closing fence closes the innermost open container, whatever its colon count:

::::tabs
:::tab First
The first tab, closed with four colons.
::::
:::tab Second
The second tab.
:::
:::

## Duplicate attributes

- Styled spans and directives with a key, an id or a class given twice, where the last one wins. Each is an error since 2.0, which the comment silences so that this document keeps passing validation:

    <!-- smd-disable-next-line attrs/duplicate -->
    [Blue text]{color=red color=blue}, :badge[Ready]{color=red color=green}, [an anchor]{#first #second} and [a note]{.note .note}.

## Conflicting titles

An error since 2.0, silenced below:

<!-- smd-disable-next-line container/title-conflict -->
:::note{title="Attribute title"} Text title
The title attribute is shown; the text after the attributes is not.
:::

